  {
   "id": "DP-01",
   "severity": "high",
   "title": "The NFL publishes no depth chart, so '2nd string' cannot be sourced",
   "detail": "https://www.nfl.com/teams/kansas-city-chiefs/depth-chart and https://www.nfl.com/depth-charts/ both return the 404 page '404 - Flag on the Play' as re-read this session. No official document assigns a player a depth rank. This namespace publishes observed starts and named replacements instead, and leaves every depth-rank cell blank.",
   "impact": "The requirement asks for 2nd/3rd/4th-string awareness. Observed starts can be built from official documents (this namespace does that); an official rank label cannot. Any page that prints '2nd string' is printing an inference.",
   "sources": [
    "https://www.nfl.com/teams/kansas-city-chiefs/depth-chart",
    "https://www.nfl.com/injuries/"
   ],
   "status": "needs review"
  },
  {
   "id": "DP-02",
   "severity": "high",
   "title": "Game Book lineups are post-game, so depth cannot be priced pre-game",
   "detail": "The Game Book is published after the game. It is ground truth for grading who actually started, but it cannot price a market. Before kickoff the only official signal is the injury report's practice and game status: who is doubtful, questionable, out.",
   "impact": "Replacement depth is gradeable after the fact and not forecastable from official sources before the fact. This is a structural limit on any strategy that wants to price a backup, and it is published rather than worked around. It is also the single largest open question in the questions register (QM-04).",
   "sources": [
    "https://static.www.nfl.com/image/upload/v1794570519/gamecenter/ab5828d9-4feb-11f1-abca-2c54536568a9.pdf",
    "https://www.nfl.com/injuries/"
   ],
   "status": "needs review"
  },
  {
   "id": "DP-03",
   "severity": "medium",
   "title": "Only one club has two consecutive graded game books this round",
   "detail": "Washington is the only club with a completed game in both week 9 and week 10 at read time, so it is the only club whose week-over-week replacement can be shown from two official Game Books. The other 31 clubs are left blank and marked uncovered. Blank is not zero.",
   "impact": "Any rate such as 'replacements per club-week' computed from this file would have n=1. No such rate is computed and none appears anywhere in this namespace.",
