  {
   "id": "DP-04",
   "severity": "medium",
   "title": "Lineup slot labels are not a stable key: three-TE and two-TE sets differ",
   "detail": "Washington started three tight ends in week 9 (J.Bates, B.Sinnott, C.Okonkwo) and two in week 10 (J.Bates, B.Sinnott), so C.Okonkwo drops out of the starting eleven while still playing 23 snaps' worth of substitute duty. Read naively, that looks like a starter being replaced. It is a formation change.",
   "impact": "A naive 'started vs did not start' diff overstates replacements. This namespace classifies that row as a rotation change and excludes it from the replacement count, with the reasoning printed on the page.",
   "sources": [
    "https://static.www.nfl.com/image/upload/v1794224919/gamecenter/ab382331-4feb-11f1-abca-2c54536568a9.pdf",
    "https://static.www.nfl.com/image/upload/v1794570519/gamecenter/ab5828d9-4feb-11f1-abca-2c54536568a9.pdf"
   ],
   "status": "needs review"
  },
  {
   "id": "DP-05",
   "severity": "high",
   "title": "Correction: a first draft of the week 9 injury block was wrong",
   "detail": "The first transcription of the Washington week-9 injury block in this namespace carried eleven names that are not on https://www.nfl.com/injuries/league/2026/reg9 (Austin Ekeler, Marshon Lattimore, Terry McLaurin, Jeremy McNichols, Samaje Perine, Bobby Wagner, Laremy Tunsil, Tress Way and three others). They were written from expectation, not from the page. The block was re-read, the real eleven rows were substituted, and the erroneous draft has been deleted from the data file.",
   "impact": "This is exactly the failure mode the brief warns about. It was caught by re-reading the source before publishing. Every other block in this namespace has now been re-read against its page the same way. The correction is published so the reader knows the check happens and can see what it caught.",
